# Synthetic execution-log fixture — T05.04 / D-0057 / R-093
# Precedence test: regression halt fires AHEAD of monotonicity even
# when the cardinality condition |F_{n+1}| >= |F_n| would otherwise
# satisfy step 2 of the 4-step ordering rule. Scenario: |F_1|=5
# with Item 3.2 PASSing, |F_2|=5 with Item 3.2 FAILing (non-
# shrinking cardinality). Both halts are eligible; the regression
# emitter exits FIRST per SKILL.md:1052-1054. The monotonicity
# step line is absent — proof that the wrapper exited before
# consulting it.
#
# This fixture intentionally mirrors the §3 fixture in D-0056
# (`fixture-regression-precedes-monotonicity.log`) from the
# regression-emitter angle: D-0056 §3 demonstrated that the
# monotonicity emitter does NOT fire on this cycle transition;
# this fixture demonstrates that the regression emitter DOES
# fire on the same transition with byte-exact payload.

CYCLE 1 START   gate=research-gate counter=1/3
CYCLE 1 END     gate=research-gate |F_1|=5 fails=[2.1,5.4,7.1,9.3,11.1] pass=[1.1,3.2,4.2,6.1,8.2,10.1]
TRANSITION 1->2 step=regression  verdict=PASS (no PASS→FAIL flips; cycle-1 PASS set = {1.1,3.2,4.2,6.1,8.2,10.1})
TRANSITION 1->2 step=monotonicity verdict=PROCEED (|F_1|=5 > 0, but cycle 2 not yet observed; loop continues into cycle 2)
CYCLE 2 START   gate=research-gate counter=2/3
CYCLE 2 END     gate=research-gate |F_2|=5 fails=[2.1,3.2,5.4,7.1,9.3] pass=[1.1,4.2,6.1,8.2,10.1,11.1]
TRANSITION 2->3 step=regression  verdict=HALT  Item 3.2 flipped PASS@1 → FAIL@2 (dedup-key=3.2; previously PASS at cycle 1, now FAIL); monotonicity step NOT consulted per SKILL.md:1054 (cardinality |F_2|=5 >= |F_1|=5 would otherwise fire)
HALT Regression detected on Item 3.2 — previously PASS at cycle 1, now FAIL. Halt overrides monotonicity check.
